:: Church encounter - feral bullied
<h1 class="ptitle"><<cabinName>></h1>
<br /><br />
/* A few settlers corner a feral nun out in the district and call her names. Any focus, feral nuns only. */
<<set _ce = setup.churchEncounters>>
<<set _fx = setup.nurseryEncounters>>
<<set _cast = _ce.cast()>>
<<if !_cast>>
	<<goto 'Youth district'>>
<<else>>
<<set _nun = _cast.nun>>
<<set _nunName = setup.displayName(_nun)>>
<<set _nHe = setup.pronounceWhat(_nun), _nHis = setup.pronounceWhos(_nun), _nHim = setup.pronounceWho(_nun)>>
<<set _carrying = either('a basket of bread for the hospital', 'an armful of clean linen for the church', 'a bucket of water from the well')>>

Halfway down the main street, you hear jeering. Three settlers have <<=_nunName>> backed up against a storehouse wall, <<=_carrying>> clutched to <<=_nHis>> chest.
<br /><br />
<<say 'Settler' setup.ImagePath+'/people/anonguy.png'>>
	Look at it, all dressed up in a habit like a person. Go on, say a prayer for us. Oh, that's right. It can't talk.
<</say>>
<br />
<<say 'Settler' setup.ImagePath+'/people/anongirl.png'>>
	Savage. They should keep it chained up with the rest of the animals, not let it walk around pretending to be holy.
<</say>>
<br />
One of them flicks at <<=_nHis>> veil. Another laughs.
<br /><br />
<<sayFeral _nun>>presses back against the boards with <<=_nHis>> shoulders hunched and <<=_nHis>> head low, teeth just showing, but holds on to <<=_carrying>> and doesn't run<</sayFeral>>
<br />

<div id="ce_choices">
	<<link `'Stand up for ' + _nHim`>>
		<<replace '#ce_choices'>>
			<<run _fx.change(_nun, 'happy', 1, 2)>>
			<<run _fx.change(_nun, 'relationship', 4, 6)>>
			<<run _ce.changePlayer('goodwill', 2)>>
			<<set _nun.churchService ??= {}>>
			<<set _nun.churchService.bullyCooldownUntil = $game.day + _ce.BULLY_COOLDOWN>>
			You step in between them and <<=_nunName>> and look at each of the settlers in turn until they stop laughing.
			<br /><br />
			<<you>>
				<<=ucfirst(_nHe)>> serves in that church every day, for every one of you. Including the ones who don't deserve it. If I hear about this again, you'll be finding somewhere else to live.
			<</you>>
			<br />
			They mutter apologies to the dirt and scatter.
			<br /><br />
			<<sayFeral _nun>>slowly straightens up, then steps close and presses <<=_nHis>> forehead to your shoulder, staying there a long moment before <<=_nHe>> trots off down the street with <<=_nHis>> head held high<</sayFeral>>
			<br />
			[[Continue|Youth district]]
			<<nurseryEffects>>
		<</replace>>
	<</link>>
	<<link 'Ignore it'>>
		<<replace '#ce_choices'>>
			<<run _fx.change(_nun, 'happy', -5, -3)>>
			<<run _fx.change(_nun, 'relationship', -6, -4)>>
			You keep walking. Behind you the jeering goes on for a while, and then stops.
			<br /><br />
			<<sayFeral _nun>>catches your eye across the street as you go, and you see the moment <<=_nHe>> understands that you aren't going to help<</sayFeral>>
			<br />
			[[Continue|Youth district]]
			<<nurseryEffects>>
		<</replace>>
	<</link>>
	<<link 'Join in'>>
		<<replace '#ce_choices'>>
			<<run _fx.change(_nun, 'happy', -10, -7)>>
			<<run _fx.change(_nun, 'relationship', -10, -7)>>
			<<run _ce.changePlayer('goodwill', -3)>>
			<<run _ce.hide(_nun)>>
			You wander over, and the settlers make room for you, grinning.
			<br /><br />
			<<you>>
				They're right, you know. You can put a dog in a dress. It's still a dog.
			<</you>>
			<br />
			The settlers howl with laughter.
			<br /><br />
			<<sayFeral _nun>>stares at you as if you had struck <<=_nHim>>, then drops <<=_carrying>> in the dirt and bolts, running flat out for the church without once looking back<</sayFeral>>
			<br />
			<<=ucfirst(_nHe)>> doesn't come out again for the rest of the day.
			<br /><br />
			[[Continue|Youth district]]
			<<nurseryEffects>>
		<</replace>>
	<</link>>
</div>
<</if>>
